// ENT-2 / ENT-8 — an entity guard covers one invariant and performs no IO; a
// reader derives state with no side effects.
//
// An entity that awaits cannot be tested without infrastructure (`ARC-TST-2`),
// and its rule becomes unavailable to anyone holding the object in memory —
// which is every caller that already loaded it.
//
// Scoped by class name rather than by the `@Entity()` decorator: Grit does not
// bind a decorated class as one pattern, and a Biome plugin cannot be limited
// to a path (the object form of `plugins` is silently ignored in 2.2.2). The
// naming convention is what makes the rule safe to run everywhere.
`class $name { $body }` where {
  $body <: contains `await $call`,
  $name <: r".*Entity$",
  register_diagnostic(
    span = $name,
    message = "ENT-2: an entity performs no IO — the rule must hold on an object already in memory."
  )
}
